      "writtenOn": "2024-10-02T18:22:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I should add more details of why to b/335431546, but what this boils down to is SkPath is already a mutable path builder, we don\u0027t need another mutable path builder. What we need is an immutable path object.\n\nThe current name of SkPath is actually just a misnomer, it is actually a mutable path builder that we then attempt to use like an immutable path. This is a holdover from when Skia was thread antagonistic and didn\u0027t really handle threading at all.",
